---
description: Verification-first workflow and multi-agent discipline
alwaysApply: true
---
For non-trivial engineering tasks, prefer the engineering-mode skill and an explicit playbook.

- Start from observable acceptance criteria.
- Investigate before editing.
- Separate implementation from independent verification.
- Use isolated worktrees/environments for concurrent writers.
- Parallelize only when ownership or judgment is genuinely independent.
- Do not use "agent says done" as a completion criterion.
- Capture commands, artifacts, metrics or reproduction evidence.
- Convert repeated failure modes into tests, lints, policies, docs, skills or tools.
